// Owns its main: it calls only root-free routes and cleans up nothing on a
// stop. Prints 3072 lines of 1024 bytes, the LF included, all from one print
// line. They fill a 65536-byte stdout buffer exactly 48 times, so a
// buffered stdout has nothing left to write at the exit.
run: fn() {
    line: "x".repeat(1023)
    loop _ in 0..<3072 -> print(line)
}
